cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this catalog, please cite it as below. Cite the specific entry and its `as of` date where possible."
title: "Silent Failure Catalog: validation that passes while nothing is being checked"
abstract: >-
  A catalog of silent failure modes in CI gates, test suites, data pipelines and
  AI-agent harnesses. Each entry names a failure pattern, gives a minimal
  reproduction, a self-check and a fix that carries a negative control.
  The shared root cause: the absence of evidence is recorded as evidence of
  absence of a problem.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Zhao"
    given-names: "Xinghua"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0512-1237"
keywords:
  - silent failure
  - false green
  - verification gap
  - CI gates
  - validation
  - test oracles
  - negative controls
  - mutation testing
  - AI agents
  - observability
